WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:13.986
Hank was hiking in the woods with his mom and his sister.

2
00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:17.747
Their dog, Sadie, was trotting beside them.

3
00:00:18.668 --> 00:00:21.049
Suddenly Sadie spotted a skunk.

4
00:00:22.149 --> 00:00:22.990
"Sadie, no!"

5
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.111
Mom shouted as Sadie bolted toward it.

6
00:00:27.071 --> 00:00:28.572
But Sadie didn't listen.

7
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.082
The skunk raised its tail.

8
00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:35.404
Sadie yelped and ran back to them.

9
00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:39.348
Her eyes were watering, and she stunk!

10
00:00:39.368 --> 00:00:42.270
"Oh no," Ella said.

11
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.792
"Sadie got sprayed!"

12
00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:48.275
They went home to give the dog a bath.

13
00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:50.157
"Skunks are mean!"

14
00:00:50.537 --> 00:00:52.879
Hank said as Mom turned on the hose.

15
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.161
Mom shrugged.

16
00:00:55.181 --> 00:00:58.204
"That skunk was just defending itself."

17
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.981
"That's right," Ella said.

18
00:01:01.001 --> 00:01:04.484
"Most animals have to protect themselves.

19
00:01:05.404 --> 00:01:07.346
Otherwise, predators will eat them."

20
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:11.169
"But rabbits don't spray Sadie," Hank said.

21
00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:12.790
"And she chases them."

22
00:01:14.351 --> 00:01:18.414
"Rabbits have a different way to defend themselves," Ella said.

23
00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:21.296
"They run fast and then hide.

24
00:01:22.216 --> 00:01:24.718
Their speed helps them escape danger."

25
00:01:25.719 --> 00:01:27.200
Mom scrubbed Sadie.

26
00:01:27.936 --> 00:01:31.158
"Can you two think of other ways animals defend themselves?"

27
00:01:32.118 --> 00:01:33.579
Hank thought for a moment.

28
00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:34.839
"I know!

29
00:01:35.279 --> 00:01:36.660
Porcupines shoot quills!"

30
00:01:38.301 --> 00:01:39.861
Ella laughed.

31
00:01:39.961 --> 00:01:45.284
"Porcupines don't actually shoot quills.

32
00:01:45.944 --> 00:01:48.765
But their quills do break off when they're attacked.

33
00:01:49.406 --> 00:01:51.227
The quills are really sharp.

34
00:01:52.007 --> 00:01:54.128
They stick into the predator's skin."

35
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.743
"That reminds me of another animal defense," Hank said.

36
00:01:58.763 --> 00:02:02.306
"Last year I learned about lizards that make their tails fall off."

37
00:02:03.647 --> 00:02:05.028
Mom looked curious.

38
00:02:05.048 --> 00:02:07.610
"How is that self-defense?"

39
00:02:08.451 --> 00:02:09.472
Hank smiled.

40
00:02:09.492 --> 00:02:14.056
"A predator that's chasing a lizard will likely grab the lizard's tail.

41
00:02:14.656 --> 00:02:17.378
So, the lizard lets it fall off and then hurries away."

42
00:02:17.398 --> 00:02:23.704
"I just thought of an animal that moves slowly," Ella said.

43
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.282
"And it doesn't have anything sharp like quills.

44
00:02:28.002 --> 00:02:30.063
But it can still protect itself."

45
00:02:31.804 --> 00:02:33.245
Hank scratched his head.

46
00:02:33.265 --> 00:02:34.545
"What is it?"

47
00:02:35.706 --> 00:02:36.547
Ella grinned.

48
00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.247
"A turtle!

49
00:02:39.068 --> 00:02:41.549
Its shell is like a suit of armor!"

50
00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:44.791
"I love turtles," Hank said.

51
00:02:44.811 --> 00:02:47.392
"But I almost stepped on one the other day.

52
00:02:47.412 --> 00:02:49.313
It blended in with the leaves."

53
00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:55.073
"So turtles have two kinds of self-defense," Mom said.

54
00:02:55.093 --> 00:02:59.215
"They have armor and camouflage to blend in."

55
00:02:59.235 --> 00:03:04.958
"Some animals protect themselves by not blending in at all," Ella said.

56
00:03:04.978 --> 00:03:07.460
"Really?" Hank asked.

57
00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.361
Ella nodded.

58
00:03:09.381 --> 00:03:12.783
"Poison frogs are bright and colorful.

59
00:03:13.523 --> 00:03:16.405
But those pretty colors are a warning.

60
00:03:17.466 --> 00:03:21.108
They tell predators, if you eat me, you'll probably die.

61
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.101
That's because their skin has deadly, toxic chemicals."

62
00:03:26.622 --> 00:03:29.483
Mom rinsed the soapy water off Sadie.

63
00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.844
The dog shivered and hung her head.

64
00:03:32.864 --> 00:03:35.305
"Poor Sadie looks so unhappy."

65
00:03:37.806 --> 00:03:38.746
Hank chuckled.

66
00:03:38.766 --> 00:03:41.728
"I bet she wishes she could defend herself from
